====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} An [[alcoholic]] [[drink]] [[ferment]]ed from [[starch]] material, commonly [[barley]] [[malt]]; often with [[hop]]s or some other [[substance]] (like [[gruit]]) to impart a [[bitter]] flavor.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:beer}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Beer''' is brewed all over the world.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=w:Ben Travers|title=w:A Cuckoo in the Nest
|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1521052W
|passage=“{{...}} the awfully hearty sort of Christmas cards that people do send to other people that they don't know at all well. You know. The kind that have mottoes like<br/>&nbsp; Here's rattling good luck and roaring good cheer, / With lashings of food and great hogsheads of '''beer'''. {{...}}”}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A fermented extract of the roots and other parts of various plants, as [[spruce]], [[ginger]], [[sassafras]], etc.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A solution produced by steeping plant materials in water or another [[fluid]].
# {{lb|en|countable}} A glass, bottle, or can of any of the above beverages.
#: {{ux|en|I bought a few '''beers''' from the shop for the party.}}
#: {{ux|en|Can I buy you a '''beer'''?}}
#: {{ux|en|I'd like two '''beers''' and a glass of white wine.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A variety of the above beverages.
#: {{ux|en|Pilsner is one of the most commonly served '''beers''' in Europe.}}
#: {{ux|en|I haven't tried this '''beer''' before.}}

